    "text": "Three rods <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BC</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BD</mi></math> of same length <math> <mrow> <mi>l</mi><mo>⁡</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;and cross section <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> are arranged as shown. The end <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> is immersed in ice whose mass is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>440</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> and is at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The end C is maintained at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. Heat is supplied at a constant rate of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cal</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Thermal conductivities of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> , <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BC</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BD</mi></math> are <math><mi>K</mi></math>, <math><mn>2</mn></math><math><mi>K</mi></math> and <math><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> , respectively. Time after which whole ice will melt is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. What is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>?&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mtext> </mtext><msup><mtext>cal&nbsp;m</mtext><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>°</mo><msup><mtext>C</mtext><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>,&nbsp;A</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mtext> </mtext><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext>m</mtext><mo>)</mo></math><br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0030680_Question.jpg\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 156px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math> <mrow> <mi>&#952;</mi> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;be the temperature of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>, then</p><p><math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mtext>KA</mtext> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mi>&#952;</mi> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mrow> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>+</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>K</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </mfenced> <mtext>A</mtext> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mi>&#952;</mi> <mo>-</mo> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mrow> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> </math></p><p>Substituting the values we obtain,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2000</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>880</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math></p><p>Rate of heat flow from <math><mi>B</mi></math> to <math><mi>D</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>0.1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>880</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>44</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><msup><mtext>cal&#160;s</mtext><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math> <mtable> <mtr> <mtd> <mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac> <mrow> <mn>440</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow> <mrow> <mn>44</mn></mrow> </mfrac> </mtd> </mtr> <mtr> <mtd> <mo>=</mo><mn>800</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mtext>s</mtext> </mtd> </mtr> </mtable> </math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p>",
